# "Until the end of your next turn": the permission of an exiled card ends with that turn. Turn 3's activation exiles
# Lightning Bolt, so its turn is turn 5; turn 5's activation exiles a Mountain, so its next turn is turn 7. On turn 7 the
# Mountain is still playable from exile (positive control, a land under the ordinary land-play rules) while the Bolt,
# whose turn ended, cannot be cast.

